      "title": "Vercel Board introduces shared message board for multi-agent workflows",
      "summary": "Vercel has released Vercel Board, an experimental message board available on all plans that provides a secure, shared space for agents to coordinate tasks, keep context together, and track completion across swarms and software factories.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Available now on all Vercel plans as an experimental feature",
        "Agents access Board via the Vercel CLI or JavaScript SDK",
        "Designed to track tasks, statuses, logs, and delegation across multiple agents"
      ],
      "design_implication": "When multiple autonomous design agents and subagents collaborate on complex design system updates, tracking progress across fragmented terminal logs creates coordination blind spots. A shared coordination primitive moves agent oversight from opaque debugging files to a visible operational surface, shifting the designer's role from inspecting single script outputs to monitoring multi-agent state. Start by mapping out what task statuses and delegation handoffs your design system agents need to surface on a shared board.",
      "implication_lens": "workflow",
      "visual_need": "illustrate",
      "source_name": "Vercel Blog",
      "source_url": "https://vercel.com/blog/introducing-vercel-board",
      "source_date": "2026-11-18T08:00:00.000Z",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "claim": "Vercel Board provides a shared message board for multi-agent workflows.",
          "quote": "It’s an experimental message board that gives agents a shared, secure place to coordinate tasks and keep context together."
        }
      ],
